#!/bin/bash
# Self-test of The Fixer, run at start-up only when the kernel command line
# has annie.selftest=fixer (the build's tests do that). It breaks a program
# and an Annie OS file on purpose, lets The Fixer find and repair them, and
# prints ANNIE-FIXER-TEST: PASS or FAIL to the console.
set -uo pipefail
say() { echo "ANNIE-FIXER-TEST: $*" | tee /dev/console /dev/ttyS0 2>/dev/null; }

say "breaking /usr/bin/nano and /usr/local/bin/annie-dc on purpose"
rm -f /usr/bin/nano
echo "broken" >>/usr/local/bin/annie-dc

list="$(mktemp)"
ANNIE_FIXER_PACKAGES="nano bash" /usr/local/bin/annie-fixer-helper scan "$list" >/dev/null
say "found: $(cut -f3 "$list" | tr '\n' ' ')"
ok=true
grep -q $'\t/usr/bin/nano$' "$list" || { say "did not notice /usr/bin/nano missing"; ok=false; }
grep -q $'\t/usr/local/bin/annie-dc$' "$list" || { say "did not notice /usr/local/bin/annie-dc damaged"; ok=false; }
grep -q '/usr/bin/bash$' "$list" && { say "wrongly reported bash as broken"; ok=false; }

/usr/local/bin/annie-fixer-helper fix "$list" | grep -v PROGRESS | while read -r l; do say "$l"; done
[[ -x /usr/bin/nano ]] && /usr/bin/nano --version >/dev/null 2>&1 || { say "nano was not put back"; ok=false; }
cmp -s /usr/local/bin/annie-dc /run/archiso/airootfs/usr/local/bin/annie-dc || { say "annie-dc was not put back"; ok=false; }

if $ok; then say PASS; else say FAIL; fi
